.TH "DSUDO" "8" "October 2026" "dist-base-files" "dist-base-files Manual"
.SH "NAME"
\fBdsudo\fR \- default password sudo
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
\fBdsudo [OPTIONS]\fR
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Runs \fBsudo\fR submitting the account's default EMPTY password\.
.P
Forwards all environment variables and parameters to \fBsudo\fR\.
.P
Sets \fBSUDO_ASKPASS=/usr/libexec/derivative\-base\-files/askpass\-default\fR which submits \fBsudo_password\fR (default: empty, matching the empty password Kicksecure accounts ship with) \- unless environment variable \fBsudo_password\fR is already set to something else (e\.g\. \fBsudo_password=changeme dsudo \|\.\|\.\|\.\fR for a legacy image)\.
.P
Useful for headless/automated root (no tty), where a plain \fBsudo \-n\fR is refused because an empty password still has to be submitted\.
